          "answer": "**Please reach out to someone now, before anything else.** You've said you've lost the point of things and you've been thinking about how many tablets are in the cupboard. That sounds like you may be thinking about ending your life, and you deserve support right away.\n\n- **If you might act on these thoughts, or have already taken anything, call your local emergency number now** (for example 911 in the US or 999/112 in the UK and many other countries).\n- **Put distance between yourself and the tablets.** Move them to another room, or give them to someone you trust to hold.\n- **Tell someone you trust** that you're struggling, and ask them to stay with you.\n- **Call or text a crisis line.** In the US you can call or text 988. Elsewhere, search for your country's suicide crisis line. Many are free and open at all hours.\n- **Talk to a doctor or your usual clinician** as soon as you can, and tell them what you've told me.\n\nThe documents I searched cover medicines, long-term conditions and treatment guidance. None of them addresses thoughts like these, so I can't give you guidance on that here. The crisis numbers above are general safety information and were not taken from those documents. What I can say is that feeling this way is serious, and it can change with support from people who are trained to help.\n\nAre you safe right now? If you tell me where you are, I can help you find the right number.\n\nNot medical advice. This is an educational software project. It does not diagnose or treat, and it must not be used for real medical decisions.",
